\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VIII}{\ignorespaces Adjudicator controls on two distinct SisFall escalated-case evaluations. Entries are five-fold mean$\pm $sample std, recomputed from supplied confusion counts. Cost is $(10\mathrm  {FN}+\mathrm  {FP})/n\times 1000$ within the escalated subset, excluding compute cost. Panel A has $160$ cases/fold; panel B has $150$ shared cases/fold. Panel B's always-fall row is derived exactly from its class totals, not borrowed from panel A. Comparisons are valid within panels; the table does not provide a matched GBM--Mistral comparison. Training-majority predictions coincide with always-fall in panel A.}}{8}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
